# neo4jaura Provider

Neo4j Aura Terraform Provider.

## Authentication

The provider supports one authentication option: **API Key**.

To obtain a client ID and secret, follow the instructions in the [Neo4j Aura documentation](https://neo4j.com/docs/aura/api/authentication/).

## Example Usage

### Programmatic Configuration

You can set the credentials directly in the provider block:

```terraform
provider "neo4jaura" {
  client_id     = "your-client-id"
  client_secret = "your-client-secret"
}
```

### Environment Variables

Alternatively, you can set the credentials via environment variables. This is often preferred for security to avoid hardcoding secrets in your configuration:

```bash
export AURA_CLIENT_ID="your-client-id"
export AURA_CLIENT_SECRET="your-client-secret"
```

When using environment variables, you can leave the provider block empty:

```terraform
provider "neo4jaura" {}
```

